' ============================================================================
'  _effects-demo.cut -- blur, desaturate and colorize, on and off.
'
'  All three run on a reduced-resolution copy of the frame, which is what makes
'  them affordable at all -- and the reduction IS the blur, so the cheapest of
'  the three is free. See CutApplyEffects.
'
'  Watch it:  cutplay.run assets/cutscenes/default/_effects-demo.cut
' ============================================================================

scene effects-demo
dev
storybook "Through A Glass" "blur, desaturate and colorize -- a filter over the picture, held until it is changed."

var body$ = "dungeon-mode.ttf"

stage 1056x816
show bg "bg/cham-armory.png" fill
cam 0.5,0.5 zoom 1

font body$ 22
color #f0e8d8

fade from black over 0.5

title "NO EFFECT" "the picture as composed" for 1.6

' BLUR. The number is the reduction factor: bigger is softer AND faster, because
' the whole filter runs on the smaller copy.
effect blur 3
title "BLUR 3" "softened by the downscale itself" for 1.6
effect blur 8
title "BLUR 8" "further down, softer still" for 1.6

' DESATURATE. Luminance-weighted, not a flat average -- a flat average turns a
' red and a blue of the same value into the same grey.
effect none
effect desaturate 1
title "DESATURATE 1" "all the colour gone, none of the detail" for 1.6

' COLORIZE. Pulls every pixel toward one colour, which is how you say
' "remembered", "poisoned" or "underwater" without new art.
effect none
effect colorize #3050ff 0.55
title "COLORIZE blue" "a memory, or deep water" for 1.6

effect none
effect desaturate 0.7
effect colorize #ff7020 0.35
effect blur 2
title "ALL THREE" "stacked -- each line sets one and leaves the rest" for 2.0

effect none
title "OFF AGAIN" "effect none clears the lot" for 1.4
fade to black over 0.8
